/* GENERATED by tools/build_pages.py from tools/recipes_data.py. Index matches MN_LISTS.snacks. */
window.MN_RECIPES = [{"slug": "graveyard-dirt-pudding", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 20 minutes</p><p>Chocolate pudding, cookie &quot;dirt&quot; and worms crawling out of the grave. The undead classic.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 box (3.9 oz) instant chocolate pudding mix</li><li>2 cups cold milk</li><li>1 cup whipped topping</li><li>15 chocolate sandwich cookies</li><li>1 cup gummy worms</li><li>Optional: cookie &quot;tombstones&quot; (oval vanilla wafers + icing pen)</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Whisk pudding mix and cold milk for 2 minutes, then chill 5 minutes until thick.</li><li>Fold in the whipped topping so the dirt is extra fluffy.</li><li>Seal the cookies in a zip bag and smash them into crumbs. Therapeutic.</li><li>Layer pudding and crumbs in cups, finishing with a thick crumb layer.</li><li>Bury gummy worms halfway so they look like they are escaping. Stick a tombstone in each.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk and wheat; cookies may contain soy. Check worm labels for gelatin.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=gummy+worms+bulk&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Gummy worms</a> · <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=halloween+dessert+cups+tombstone&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Tombstone dessert cups</a></p>"}, {"slug": "bloody-popcorn", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 10 minutes</p><p>Buttery popcorn splattered like the third act of a slasher.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>10 cups popped popcorn (about 1/2 cup kernels)</li><li>3 tbsp butter, melted</li><li>1/4 cup strawberry syrup (ice cream topping)</li><li>1/2 tsp salt</li><li>Optional: red candy melts for thicker &quot;blood&quot;</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Spread popcorn on a sheet pan lined with parchment.</li><li>Toss with melted butter and salt.</li><li>Drizzle strawberry syrup across in thin splatters with a spoon (flick your wrist for crime-scene realism).</li><li>Let it set 5 minutes, then pile into a bowl and serve fast before it gets soggy.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk (butter). Use plant butter for dairy-free.</p>"}, {"slug": "mummy-hot-dogs", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 25 minutes</p><p>Hot dogs wrapped in pastry bandages. They rise from the oven, as is tradition.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>8 hot dogs</li><li>1 can (8 oz) crescent roll dough</li><li>Mustard or ketchup for eyes</li><li>Optional: candy eyes (stick on after baking)</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment.</li><li>Cut dough into thin strips and wrap each dog like a mummy, leaving a gap near one end for the face.</li><li>Bake 12-15 minutes until golden and the hot dogs are heated through.</li><li>Dot on mustard eyes, cool 2 minutes and serve. Cut into small pieces for little kids (hot dogs are a choking hazard).</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat; dough may contain milk and soy.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=candy+eyeballs+edible&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Candy eyes</a></p>"}, {"slug": "candy-corn-snack-mix", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 8 · about 5 minutes</p><p>Candy corn is divisive. Hide it in salty mix so even the haters eat it.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>2 cups candy corn</li><li>2 cups salted peanuts (or pretzel pieces for nut-free)</li><li>2 cups mini pretzels</li><li>1 cup chocolate candies</li><li>1 cup popcorn</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Dump everything into a big bowl.</li><li>Toss with your hands like you are mixing a potion.</li><li>Serve in a cauldron. Accept no complaints about the ending.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains peanuts (swap for pretzels or roasted chickpeas to make it nut-free), wheat, milk and soy. Many candies are made in facilities with nuts.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=candy+corn+bulk&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Candy corn</a></p>"}, {"slug": "witch-finger-pretzels", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 20 minutes</p><p>Pretzel rods dipped in green candy, with an almond fingernail. Gnarly, crunchy, cursed.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>12 pretzel rods</li><li>1 cup green candy melts</li><li>12 whole almonds (or red candy-coated chocolates for nut-free)</li><li>Optional: black sprinkles for warts</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Melt candy melts in the microwave in 30-second bursts, stirring each time.</li><li>Dip the top two-thirds of each pretzel rod and tap off the extra.</li><li>Press an almond on the tip as the nail. Pinch a little extra coating into &quot;knuckles&quot;.</li><li>Lay on parchment and chill 10 minutes until set.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains tree nuts (almonds), wheat, and milk/soy in candy melts. Use a chocolate candy nail for a nut-free hand.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=green+candy+melts&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Green candy melts</a></p>"}, {"slug": "witchs-cauldron-cheese-puffs", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 5 minutes</p><p>The recipe is the bowl. Bigger. Bigger. Okay, that is suspicious.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 family-size bag cheese puffs</li><li>1 tsp smoked paprika or taco seasoning</li><li>Optional: 1/2 cup pumpkin-shaped candies</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Pour the cheese puffs into the largest bowl you own (a cauldron is ideal).</li><li>Sprinkle paprika over the top and shake gently for a spicy &quot;dragon dust&quot; upgrade.</li><li>Hand out napkins, or accept orange fingerprints on the remote forever.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Usually contains milk; check the bag for wheat and soy.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=halloween+cauldron+serving+bowl&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Plastic cauldron bowl</a></p>"}, {"slug": "pizza-bagels", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 15 minutes</p><p>Rad, tubular, and ready during the opening credits.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>4 plain bagels, split</li><li>1 cup pizza sauce</li><li>2 cups shredded mozzarella</li><li>Mini pepperoni or sliced olives</li><li>1 tsp Italian seasoning</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 425°F (220°C). Put bagel halves cut-side up on a baking sheet.</li><li>Spread sauce, pile on cheese and add pepperoni or olive &quot;eyes&quot;.</li><li>Sprinkle Italian seasoning.</li><li>Bake 8-10 minutes until the cheese bubbles. Cool 2 minutes so it doesn&#x27;t burn your mouth.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat and milk.</p>"}, {"slug": "eyeball-meatballs", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 25 minutes</p><p>Meatballs that stare back. Mozzarella and olive eyes in a pool of red.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 bag (about 24) frozen fully cooked meatballs</li><li>1 jar (24 oz) marinara sauce</li><li>12 small mozzarella pearls, halved</li><li>6 black olives, sliced</li><li>Toothpicks for serving</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Simmer the meatballs in marinara in a covered pan for 15 minutes, stirring now and then, until hot all the way through (165°F/74°C).</li><li>Turn off the heat and press a mozzarella half on top of each meatball.</li><li>Put an olive slice in the middle as a pupil.</li><li>Cover 1 minute so the cheese sticks, then serve with toothpicks.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk; frozen meatballs often contain wheat and egg (cooked).</p>"}, {"slug": "brain-jello", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 8 · about 20 minutes</p><p>A wobbly pink brain. Plus 4 hours of chill time while it thinks about what it did.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>2 boxes (6 oz each) peach or watermelon gelatin</li><li>2 cups boiling water</li><li>1 can (12 oz) evaporated milk</li><li>1-2 drops green food coloring (for a grayish-pink brain)</li><li>Cooking spray</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Lightly spray a brain mold (about 6 cups).</li><li>Stir gelatin into boiling water for 2 minutes until fully dissolved.</li><li>Stir in evaporated milk and a drop of green color for that gray matter look.</li><li>Pour into the mold and chill at least 4 hours until firm.</li><li>Dip the mold in warm water for 10 seconds and flip onto a plate. Jiggle ominously.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk. Gelatin is not vegetarian; use an agar dessert mix if needed.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=brain+gelatin+mold&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Brain gelatin mold</a></p>"}, {"slug": "roasted-pumpkin-seeds", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 30 minutes</p><p>Rescue the guts from your jack-o&#x27;-lantern and turn them into crunchy little coffin nails.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 1/2 cups pumpkin seeds, rinsed and patted dry</li><li>1 tbsp olive oil or melted butter</li><li>1/2 tsp salt</li><li>1/2 tsp garlic powder or cinnamon sugar</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 325°F (165°C).</li><li>Pick off the stringy pulp, rinse the seeds and dry them well on a towel.</li><li>Toss with oil, salt and seasoning, then spread in one layer on a baking sheet.</li><li>Roast 20-25 minutes, stirring halfway, until golden and crunchy. Cool before snacking.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Pumpkin seeds are seeds, not tree nuts, but check if anyone has a seed allergy. Butter adds milk.</p>"}, {"slug": "bat-wings", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 50 minutes</p><p>Sticky, dark and glossy. Black-as-night glaze, zero actual bats.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>2 lb chicken wings</li><li>1 tbsp oil</li><li>1/2 cup barbecue sauce</li><li>2 tbsp soy sauce</li><li>1 tbsp honey</li><li>Salt and pepper</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 425°F (220°C) and line a sheet pan with foil and a rack.</li><li>Pat wings dry, toss with oil, salt and pepper, and bake 40-45 minutes, flipping once, until crisp and 165°F (74°C) inside.</li><li>Stir barbecue sauce, soy sauce and honey in a bowl.</li><li>Toss hot wings in the glaze and bake 5 more minutes until sticky.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains soy and usually wheat (soy sauce). Wash hands and surfaces after handling raw chicken.</p>"}, {"slug": "swamp-water", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 5 minutes</p><p>Murky green and full of frogs. Tastes way better than it looks.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 liter lime or lemon-lime soda, chilled</li><li>2 cups limeade</li><li>1 cup ice</li><li>1 cup gummy frogs</li><li>Optional: a few drops blue food coloring for a darker swamp</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Pour the soda and limeade into a pitcher or punch bowl over ice.</li><li>Add a drop or two of blue coloring for that bog-green color.</li><li>Drop gummy frogs in right before serving so they swim, not dissolve.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Most gummies contain gelatin. Small gummies can be a choking risk for little kids.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=gummy+frogs&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Gummy frogs</a></p>"}, {"slug": "ghost-meringues", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 8 · about 120 minutes</p><p>Little baked ghosts that melt on your tongue. Silent, mostly.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>3 large egg whites, room temperature (or 1/2 cup pasteurized egg whites)</li><li>3/4 cup sugar</li><li>1/4 tsp cream of tartar</li><li>1 tsp vanilla</li><li>Mini chocolate chips for eyes</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 225°F (110°C) and line two baking sheets with parchment.</li><li>Beat egg whites and cream of tartar until foamy, then add sugar a spoonful at a time and beat until stiff and glossy. Beat in vanilla.</li><li>Pipe tall ghost swirls with a zip bag with the corner cut off. Add two chocolate chip eyes.</li><li>Bake 90 minutes until dry and crisp (fully baked, not raw), then turn off the oven and let them cool inside.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains egg. Chocolate chips may contain milk and soy.</p>"}, {"slug": "caramel-apples", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 30 minutes</p><p>Shiny, sticky and only slightly cursed. Melting store caramels keeps it easy and safe.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>6 small crisp apples (Granny Smith is great)</li><li>1 bag (11 oz) soft caramels, unwrapped</li><li>2 tbsp milk or cream</li><li>6 sturdy sticks</li><li>Toppings: crushed cookies, sprinkles or chopped peanuts</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Wash and dry the apples well (wax keeps caramel from sticking). Push a stick into each.</li><li>Microwave caramels and milk in 30-second bursts, stirring, until smooth. It is very hot, so adults handle this part.</li><li>Dip and twirl each apple, letting extra drip off.</li><li>Roll in toppings and set on buttered parchment. Chill 15 minutes until firm.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk. Peanut topping contains nuts, so offer a nut-free sprinkle option.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=caramel+apple+sticks&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Caramel apple sticks</a></p>"}, {"slug": "licorice-graveyard-board", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 5 minutes</p><p>A snack board of dark candy for the brave, with a safety note even ghouls should know.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>8 oz black licorice twists or bites</li><li>1 cup dark chocolate pieces</li><li>1 cup blackberries</li><li>1 cup pretzels</li><li>Optional: red licorice for the cowards</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Arrange everything on a board in spooky piles.</li><li>Cut licorice twists into &quot;bones&quot; and cross them like a skull flag.</li><li>Snack in moderation: the FDA warns that eating a lot of black licorice daily for weeks can affect heart rhythm, especially for adults over 40.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Licorice usually contains wheat. Chocolate may contain milk and soy.</p>"}, {"slug": "unholy-nachos", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 15 minutes</p><p>Sheet-pan nachos so spicy the priest leaves early.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 bag (11 oz) tortilla chips</li><li>2 cups shredded cheddar or Mexican blend</li><li>1 can (15 oz) black beans, drained</li><li>1/2 cup sliced jalapeños (pickled or fresh)</li><li>Salsa, sour cream and guacamole for dunking</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 400°F (200°C) and spread chips on a parchment-lined sheet pan.</li><li>Scatter beans, cheese and an unholy amount of jalapeños.</li><li>Bake 6-8 minutes until the cheese melts.</li><li>Serve with salsa, sour cream and guac. Wash hands after cutting fresh jalapeños and don&#x27;t touch your eyes.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk. Check chips if anyone avoids corn.</p>"}, {"slug": "severed-finger-cookies", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 12 · about 30 minutes</p><p>Knobby sugar cookie fingers with almond nails and jam &quot;blood&quot;. Gross, perfect.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 tube (16.5 oz) refrigerated sugar cookie dough</li><li>1/4 cup flour (to make the dough easy to shape)</li><li>24 whole almonds (or chocolate chips for nut-free)</li><li>1/4 cup strawberry jam</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 350°F (175°C). Knead flour into the dough.</li><li>Roll tablespoon-size pieces into finger shapes and pinch in two knuckles; score lines with a knife.</li><li>Press an almond on one end as a nail.</li><li>Bake 10-12 minutes until the edges barely brown. Cool, then lift the nail and dab jam underneath and on the cut end.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains tree nuts (almonds), wheat, egg and milk (cookie dough). Use chocolate chip nails for nut-free.</p>"}, {"slug": "toxic-green-slime-punch", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 10 · about 10 minutes</p><p>A glowing green potion that fizzes like a lab accident. Ladle carefully, the worms bite back.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1/2 gallon (1.9 L) lime sherbet</li><li>2 liters lemon-lime soda, chilled</li><li>4 cups (32 oz) pineapple juice, chilled</li><li>1 cup gummy worms</li><li>Optional: 1 drop green food coloring for extra glow</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Scoop the lime sherbet into a big punch bowl and let it soften for 5 minutes.</li><li>Pour in the pineapple juice, then slowly add the soda so it foams up like toxic sludge.</li><li>Stir gently and add a drop of green coloring if it isn&#x27;t radioactive enough.</li><li>Hang gummy worms over the rim and drop a few in. Serve right away while it&#x27;s frothy.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk (sherbet). Gummy worms usually contain gelatin. Use a dairy-free sorbet for vegan ghouls.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=gummy+worms&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Gummy worms</a> · <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=halloween+punch+bowl&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Halloween punch bowl</a></p>"}, {"slug": "raccoon-pizza", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 2 · about 5 minutes</p><p>Cold pizza is valid. But a 5-minute skillet crisp turns raccoon food into something legendary.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>4 slices leftover pizza (refrigerated within 2 hours of delivery and eaten within 3-4 days)</li><li>Optional: chili flakes, honey or ranch for dunking</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Eat it cold, straight from the fridge, like a raccoon. Or:</li><li>Put slices in a dry nonstick skillet over medium heat for 2 minutes until the bottom crisps.</li><li>Add a few drops of water to the pan away from the slices, cover with a lid for 1 minute to melt the cheese.</li><li>Drizzle with hot honey and chili flakes. Eat in the dark.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat and milk.</p>"}, {"slug": "coffin-grilled-cheese", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 15 minutes</p><p>Melty grilled cheese cut into coffins. Perfect with tomato soup &quot;blood&quot;.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>8 slices sandwich bread</li><li>8 slices cheddar or American cheese</li><li>2 tbsp softened butter</li><li>Optional: tomato soup for dipping</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Cut the bread into coffin shapes with a knife (trim the corners into a long hexagon) or a coffin cookie cutter.</li><li>Butter the outsides and sandwich cheese (trimmed to fit) in the middle.</li><li>Cook in a skillet over medium-low heat 2-3 minutes per side until golden and melty.</li><li>Serve with a mug of tomato soup for dunking. Save the bread scraps for croutons.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat and milk.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=coffin+cookie+cutter&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Coffin cookie cutter</a></p>"}, {"slug": "taz-style-mocktail", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 5 minutes</p><p>Taz chugs four energy drinks a night. Please don&#x27;t. Here is a caffeine-free fizz with the same neon chaos.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>2 cups sparkling water or ginger ale</li><li>1 cup white grape juice</li><li>1/2 cup mango or passion fruit juice</li><li>Juice of 1 lime</li><li>Ice and lime wheels</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Fill four glasses with ice.</li><li>Divide the juices and lime juice between them.</li><li>Top with sparkling water and stir.</li><li>Garnish with a lime wheel and scream &quot;TAZ MODE&quot; with zero jitters.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: No common allergens. Caffeine-free, so it&#x27;s safe for kids and late-night movies.</p>"}, {"slug": "grave-hogs-mystery-chili", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 45 minutes</p><p>Grave Hog says it is a family secret. It is beef, beans and a little cocoa. Don&#x27;t tell him we told you.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 lb ground beef or turkey</li><li>1 onion, diced</li><li>2 cans (15 oz) kidney or black beans, drained</li><li>1 can (28 oz) crushed tomatoes</li><li>3 tbsp chili powder, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp salt</li><li>1 tbsp cocoa powder (the mystery)</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Brown the meat and onion in a large pot over medium-high heat until no pink remains (160°F/71°C). Drain fat.</li><li>Stir in spices and cocoa for 1 minute.</li><li>Add tomatoes and beans, bring to a simmer.</li><li>Simmer 30 minutes, stirring now and then. Serve with cheese, sour cream or chips. Do not ask.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Free of the top allergens as written; toppings may add milk or wheat.</p>"}, {"slug": "riff-rot-coffee", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 10 minutes</p><p>Dark as a tour van at 3 a.m. Riff-Rot drinks it black; you can add whatever you want, we won&#x27;t tell.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>6 tbsp medium-coarse ground coffee (or decaf for late movies)</li><li>4 cups hot water (just off the boil, about 200°F/93°C)</li><li>Optional: a pinch of cinnamon in the grounds</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Add coffee (and cinnamon) to a French press or drip machine.</li><li>Pour in the hot water and stir; brew 4 minutes in a French press.</li><li>Press slowly and pour into the blackest mugs you own.</li><li>Serve decaf after 8 p.m. so you can actually sleep after the movie.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: No common allergens. Not for kids: contains caffeine unless you use decaf.</p>"}, {"slug": "spider-web-brownies", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 16 · about 45 minutes</p><p>Fudgy brownies with a white icing web. Add a plastic spider if you hate your friends.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 box brownie mix plus the eggs, oil and water it calls for</li><li>1/2 cup white icing or melted white chocolate</li><li>Optional: candy spiders or a chocolate candy body</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Bake brownies in a 9x13 pan as the box says until a toothpick comes out with moist crumbs (don&#x27;t eat raw batter: raw egg and flour).</li><li>Cool completely, about 30 minutes.</li><li>Pipe 4 rings of icing, then drag a toothpick from the center out to make the web.</li><li>Add a candy spider, cut into squares and serve.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat, egg and milk; may contain soy and be made near nuts.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=edible+candy+spiders&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Halloween spider decorations</a></p>"}, {"slug": "pigs-in-coffins", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 25 minutes</p><p>Tiny sausages tucked in for eternal sleep.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 pack (12-14 oz) cocktail sausages</li><li>1 can (8 oz) crescent dough</li><li>Mustard for dipping</li><li>1 tbsp sesame seeds (optional)</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oven to 375°F (190°C).</li><li>Cut dough into small rectangles and lay a sausage on each.</li><li>Wrap the &quot;blanket&quot; up to the sausage&#x27;s chin so the head pokes out. Sprinkle seeds.</li><li>Bake 12-15 minutes until golden. Serve with mustard. Cut for small kids.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat; dough may contain milk and soy. Sesame seeds are a common allergen, so leave them off if needed.</p>"}, {"slug": "candy-bar-bark", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 10 · about 20 minutes</p><p>Turn the mountain into candy bar bark: melted chocolate studded with chopped fun-size loot.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>12 oz semisweet chocolate chips</li><li>2 cups chopped fun-size candy bars</li><li>1/4 cup Halloween sprinkles</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Line a sheet pan with parchment.</li><li>Melt chocolate in the microwave in 30-second bursts, stirring until smooth.</li><li>Spread it about 1/4 inch thick and scatter candy pieces and sprinkles, pressing lightly.</li><li>Chill 15 minutes, then smash into jagged shards.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk and soy; many candy bars contain peanuts, tree nuts or wheat. Check every wrapper if allergies are in the crypt.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=halloween+sprinkles&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Halloween sprinkles</a></p>"}, {"slug": "kettle-corn", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 10 minutes</p><p>Sweet, salty and crackling like a carnival after closing time.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1/4 cup vegetable oil</li><li>1/2 cup popcorn kernels</li><li>1/4 cup sugar</li><li>1/2 tsp salt</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Heat oil and 3 kernels in a large pot with a lid over medium heat until they pop.</li><li>Add the rest of the kernels and the sugar, stir, and cover.</li><li>Shake the pot constantly as it pops so the sugar doesn&#x27;t burn. Remove from heat when popping slows to 2-3 seconds apart.</li><li>Dump onto a sheet pan right away, sprinkle with salt and let cool. Melted sugar is very hot, so adults only at the stove.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: No common allergens. Whole popcorn is a choking risk for kids under 4.</p>"}, {"slug": "lava-salsa", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 6 · about 10 minutes</p><p>A fiery red blender salsa that erupts out of the bowl.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 can (14.5 oz) fire-roasted tomatoes</li><li>1/2 small onion</li><li>1 garlic clove</li><li>1 jalapeño (seeds removed for mild)</li><li>Juice of 1 lime, 1/4 cup cilantro, 1/2 tsp salt</li><li>1 bag tortilla chips</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Put tomatoes, onion, garlic, jalapeño, lime, cilantro and salt in a blender.</li><li>Pulse 5-8 times until chunky, not soup.</li><li>Taste and add more jalapeño for more lava.</li><li>Serve in a bowl with a ring of bone-dry chips.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: No common allergens. Check chips if anyone avoids corn.</p>"}, {"slug": "vampire-bite-cupcakes", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 12 · about 45 minutes</p><p>Pale frosted cupcakes with two fang holes oozing raspberry.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 box white or vanilla cake mix plus the eggs, oil and water it calls for</li><li>1/2 cup seedless raspberry jam</li><li>1 tub (16 oz) vanilla frosting</li><li>A straw for making bite marks</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Bake cupcakes as the box says (until a toothpick comes out clean) and cool completely.</li><li>Use a small spoon to scoop a little hole in each top and fill with jam.</li><li>Frost smoothly over the top.</li><li>Poke two fang holes with a straw and drip a tiny bit of jam from each. Dramatic.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains wheat, egg and milk; may contain soy.</p><p class=\"rec-shop\">Shop the specialty stuff: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=halloween+cupcake+liners&amp;tag=thejurn-20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\">Halloween cupcake liners</a></p>"}, {"slug": "full-size-candy-bar-sundae", "html": "<p class=\"rec-meta\">Serves 4 · about 10 minutes</p><p>Live like the rich neighbors: chop a full-size bar over an ice cream sundae.</p><h4>Ingredients</h4><ul><li>1 pint vanilla ice cream</li><li>2 full-size candy bars, chopped</li><li>1/4 cup chocolate or caramel sauce</li><li>Whipped cream</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Scoop ice cream into four bowls.</li><li>Drizzle with sauce.</li><li>Pile on chopped candy bars and a swirl of whipped cream.</li><li>Keep one bar whole and unopened. Display it like a trophy.</li></ol><p class=\"rec-allergen\">⚠ Allergens: Contains milk and soy; many candy bars contain peanuts, tree nuts or wheat.</p>"}];
